 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-003\", \"clauses\": {\"determine_place_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F21\", \"template\": \"What is the {pv_label} of the digit {digit} in {number}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F21 asks for the place value of a digit in a number. pv_label is drawn from F01, which prints the word \\\"place value\\\".\"}, \"domain_2_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F21\", \"template\": \"What is the {pv_label} of the digit {digit} in {number}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The number slot of F21 prints 10, 12, 15, 20 and 50, all 2-digit numbers, so the range clause is addressed.\"}, \"determine_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 asks whether a stated value of a digit in a place is correct. F19 prints it as a True or False question, so it addresses the value of a digit.\"}, \"determine_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 asks for the digit of a given 2-digit number in a given place name, which is the digit of a number given its place value.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F13\", \"F14\", \"F17\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Count from the right: {relevant_places}.\", \"Look at the digits of {number} from the right: {relevant_places}.\", \"Multiply it by its place: {digit} × {v} = {value}.\", \"{p0}\", \"{p0}, {p1}\", \"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"(1) F07 prints a multiplication operation (\\\"Multiply it by its place\\\", the × sign), and \\\"multiplication\\\" is in NOT_YET_KNOWN. (2) F13 draws from the PLACE_NAMES list, which includes \\\"hundreds\\\" (NOT_YET_KNOWN) and \\\"thousands\\\" (a 4-digit place), with no derived_from_values bounding it to the 2-digit number. F13 appears in correct_answer and format_data.mcq_options, so a 2-digit place question can key \\\"hundreds\\\" or \\\"thousands\\\". (3) F14 uses the same PLACE_NAMES domain, is distinct per render, and is nested in F03 and F06. F03 and F06 print relevant_places from F13 and F14, so hints can print \\\"hundreds\\\" or \\\"thousands\\\" for a 2-digit number. F15 is restricted to ones and tens and is not at fault. (4) F17 is a 16-word sentence (\\\"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\\\" with 2-digit, single-digit and place slots), which exceeds sentence_max_words 15. F19 prints it as question_text. Its fill_value distractors (for example 5 or 4) are not constrained by digit and place, so a member can equal the true value and make a statement labelled false actually true. This is a risk the domains allow, not a proven fault. F18 and F22 were checked and not failed. The 'in, in' wording in F22 is awkward but readable.\"}",
